  "uniform_gain_invariants": {
    "bs1770": "Before integer requantization, K-weighted block energy scales by gain squared, every block loudness and both absolute/relative program loudness shift by selected_gain_db. Relative-gate membership is invariant. The measured minimum block margins prove the absolute -70 LUFS membership remains invariant. V2 must nevertheless remeasure decoded output.",
    "sample_peak": "Before requantization, sample peak dBFS shifts exactly by selected_gain_db. PCM24 predicted integer maxima are far below saturation; decoded output must be measured again.",
    "true_peak": "The version-frozen 8x cubic-Hermite reconstruction is linear, so before requantization true peak shifts exactly by selected_gain_db. V2 must rerun the same true-peak implementation over quantized output.",
    "boundary_seam": "Both stereo endpoint frames are exact zero. Uniform gain and round-to-nearest preserve exact zero, so boundary jump remains exact zero (-300 dBFS report floor).",
    "head_tail_rms_delta": "Equal gain cancels from the head/tail RMS ratio, so the delta is invariant before requantization.",
    "zero_crossing_rate": "Positive uniform gain preserves signs before requantization. PCM24 rounding may map extremely small values to zero, therefore the actual proxy must be recomputed rather than asserted byte-for-byte invariant.",
    "first_difference_rms_delta": "Equal gain cancels from the head/tail first-difference RMS ratio before requantization; actual quantized output must be recomputed.",
    "duration_format_channels": "A data-value-only mapping cannot change frame count, sample rate, bit depth, channel count, RIFF layout or full-file loop contract; validator must enforce all fields and non-data bytes."
  },
